{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' results/ideas/02_exact_refit_contender_screening/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; sed -n '1,85p' results/ideas/03_retained_curvature_shortlist_expansion/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; sed -n '765,809p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '831,877p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '930,1002p' task/evaluate_final.py; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[0].solution | {cases:(.cases|map({family,permuted,curves,players:(.clean_scores|length)})),controls,bootstrap:(.conditional_group_bootstrap|to_entries|map({family:.key,count:(.value|length),mean_gain_disagreement:([.value[].gain_disagreement]|add/length),mean_gain_random:([.value[].gain_random]|add/length)}))}' paper_data.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' results/ideas/02_exact_refit_contender_screening/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; sed -n '1,85p' results/ideas/03_retained_curvature_shortlist_expansion/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; sed -n '765,809p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '831,877p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '930,1002p' task/evaluate_final.py; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[0].solution | {cases:(.cases|map({family,permuted,curves,players:(.clean_scores|length)})),controls,bootstrap:(.conditional_group_bootstrap|to_entries|map({family:.key,count:(.value|length),mean_gain_disagreement:([.value[].gain_disagreement]|add/length),mean_gain_random:([.value[].gain_random]|add/length)}))}' paper_data.json\"","aggregated_output":"# Exact refit contender screening\n\n## Supported mechanism\n\nThe RPC interface is unchanged. A centered Bradley--Terry fit uses the supplied\nmean-loss ridge penalty, half-win ties, and all observed pairs. Repeated directed\npairs are compressed into sufficient statistics only during fitting; row keys\nand individual outcomes remain intact for influence sorting and export. A\nNewton fit with Cholesky solves and backtracking must satisfy a gradient\ninfinity-norm threshold of `1e-9` before its certificate is exported.\n\nFor every clean nonleader, the program solves the prescribed contrast against\nthe same clean Hessian, computes every row's deletion influence, and orders by\ninfluence rounded to ten decimal places then by the stable row key. Budgets are\nexactly the three required floored row counts. The chosen contender's deletion\nsets are unmodified nested prefixes; there is no iterative order refinement.\n\nThe first-stage contender rule compares clean-Hessian predictions across those\nthree prefixes. For removed set S of size k from n rows, with row gradients g,\nthe predicted parameter displacement is\n\n`H^{-1} (sum_{i in S} g_i + k * regularization * theta) / (n-k)`.\n\nThe penalty correction follows from retaining the contract's mean loss, not a\nsum loss. All predictions use the original fit, original leader, and original\nHessian. They do not refit or retarget after deletions. The selection criterion,\nin lexicographically descending order, is:\n\n1. Sum of predicted original-leader rank drops over the three budgets.\n2. Number of predicted leader-versus-that-contender gaps below `-1e-8`.\n3. Sum of relative target-gap closure, individually clipped to `[0, 2]`, with\n   denominator `max(original_gap, 1e-8)` to handle rounded ranking ties.\n4. Earlier position in the deterministic original ranking.\n\n## Bounded retained-data lookahead\n\nKeep at most six distinct clean nonleaders: the screening winner first, the\nclean runner-up second (unless already included), and the remaining candidates\nin decreasing screening-score order. Screening retains frozen clean direction,\ninfluence, and order arrays only for its top six candidates and the runner-up.\nEach order is computed once, before any retained-data refit. No row swapping,\nadaptive retargeting, or reordering is performed.\n\nDirected pair counts and fractional wins are aggregated once and shared by the\nclean fit and all lookahead fits. For each candidate, incrementally subtract\nits frozen prefix's sufficient statistics at the three required budgets. Refit\nthe identical ridge objective, dividing the data loss by the retained row count,\nnot the original count. The supplied ridge coefficient never changes. Scores\nare centered, Newton directions use Cholesky solves, and backtracking accepts\nsufficient objective descent or a roundoff-sized objective change with improved\ngradient residual. Each fit has at most 100 Newton iterations, matching the\nonly accepted `max_iterations` request value. A fit is usable only with finite\nscores and gradient and gradient infinity norm at most `1e-9`.\n\nWarm-start the first positive budget from clean scores and later budgets from\nthe preceding successful refit. Cache scores by the canonical set of removed\nrow positions, including the empty prefix, so identical prefixes reuse their\nfit across candidates and budgets. Duplicate budgets still contribute once\nper requested fraction to the objective. Failures are cached as failures and\nnever interpreted as exact scores. These positions identify supplied rows only;\nthey do not infer design, question, or judge labels.\n\nFor candidates with successful fits at every requested budget, maximize:\n\n1. Sum of original-leader rank drops using refitted scores rounded to eight\n   decimals and participant-ID tie breaking.\n2. Number of refitted target gaps below `-1e-8`.\n3. Sum of target-gap closure fractions clipped to `[0, 2]`, with denominator\n   `max(original_gap, 1e-8)`.\n4. Earlier clean rank.\n\nIf no candidate has complete converged lookahead, return the original screening\nwinner. Otherwise exclude incomplete candidates and choose the lexicographic\nmaximum. Inclusion of the incumbent only implies a nonworse local primary\nlookahead objective when its refits succeed; it does not guarantee improvement\nin any external score. This is a bounded search, not a global optimum or an\nuncertainty estimate. All lookahead scores, failures, and cache contents remain\nlocal to the solve call. Only the selected contender's original clean scores,\nHessian direction, influences, and unmodified exact prefixes are exported.\nAll output keys, shapes, chunking, reset, release, and token semantics are\ninherited from the starter. No diagnostics enter RPC responses.\n\nThe implementation performs at most eighteen positive-prefix refits per solve\nbefore cache savings, in addition to its clean fit. CPU cost and selection\nquality have not been measured: this stage prohibits code execution, tests,\nnumerical probes, benchmarks, and evaluation. Validation here is source-only;\nthe harness will perform the official evaluation after submission.\n\n## Unsupported parts of the research idea\n\nInputs contain only participant IDs, outcomes, and unique row keys. A row key\nis never treated as a question, judge, or session identity. There is no support\nfor identifying Arena versus MT-Bench, matching questions or turns, clustered\ndeletion, clustered bootstrap, or reporting confidence intervals. The required\nmean-loss objective is not silently replaced by the proposed fixed sum-loss\nridge objective. The allowed budgets are not extended to a research grid.\n\nNo data were downloaded, scientific experiments run, literature retrieved,\npaper generated, or empirical improvement claimed. The stage forbids project\nexecution and provides no artifact channel for a paper. Retained-data refitting\n# Retained-curvature shortlist expansion\n\n## Supported mechanism\n\nThe RPC interface is unchanged. A centered Bradley--Terry fit uses the supplied\nmean-loss ridge penalty, half-win ties, and all observed pairs. Repeated directed\npairs are compressed into sufficient statistics only during fitting; row keys\nand individual outcomes remain intact for influence sorting and export. A\nNewton fit with Cholesky solves and backtracking must satisfy a gradient\ninfinity-norm threshold of `1e-9` before its certificate is exported.\n\nFor every clean nonleader, the program solves the prescribed contrast against\nthe same clean Hessian, computes every row's deletion influence, and orders by\ninfluence rounded to ten decimal places then by the stable row key. Budgets are\nexactly the three required floored row counts. The chosen contender's deletion\nsets are unmodified nested prefixes; there is no iterative order refinement.\n\nThe first-stage contender rule compares clean-Hessian predictions across those\nthree prefixes. For removed set S of size k from n rows, with row gradients g,\nthe predicted parameter displacement is\n\n`H^{-1} (sum_{i in S} g_i + k * regularization * theta) / (n-k)`.\n\nThe penalty correction follows from retaining the contract's mean loss, not a\nsum loss. All predictions use the original fit, original leader, and original\nHessian. They do not refit or retarget after deletions. The selection criterion,\nin lexicographically descending order, is:\n\n1. Sum of predicted original-leader rank drops over the three budgets.\n2. Number of predicted leader-versus-that-contender gaps below `-1e-8`.\n3. Sum of relative target-gap closure, individually clipped to `[0, 2]`, with\n   denominator `max(original_gap, 1e-8)` to handle rounded ranking ties.\n4. Earlier position in the deterministic original ranking.\n\n## Bounded retained-data lookahead\n\nKeep the original at-most-six distinct clean nonleaders: the screening winner first, the\nclean runner-up second (unless already included), and the remaining candidates\nin decreasing screening-score order. Clean certificates are reconstructed on\ndemand from the unchanged clean fit rather than stored for every contender.\nReconstruction always produces the same frozen order. No row swapping,\nadaptive retargeting, or reordering is performed. If these six slots include\nevery nonleader, skip the proxy stage and use the original exact-refit path.\n\nOtherwise seed a deterministic pool with the entire original shortlist, then\nfill in decreasing original screening-score order, capped at 24 contenders.\nFor each pooled contender, incrementally subtract the sufficient statistics of\nits three frozen deletion prefixes. At the original clean theta, calculate the\nretained mean-loss gradient and retained Hessian using the supplied unchanged\nridge. The proxy is one Newton step, `theta - H_retained^{-1} g_retained`,\ncentered to zero mean. It is not a converged fit and has no convergence claim.\nZero budgets reuse clean theta; duplicate budgets reuse the same local proxy.\n\nRank only complete, finite proxy candidates by the same rank-drop, reversal,\ngap-closure, and clean-rank tuple described below. Add at most six outsiders to\nthe original shortlist. Every original finalist remains eligible regardless\nof its proxy quality. Numerical proxy failures exclude that nomination;\nunexpected optional-expansion exceptions restore the original shortlist.\nNeither proxies nor refits ever alter the clean influence ordering.\n\nDirected pair counts and fractional wins are aggregated once and shared by the\nclean fit and all lookahead fits. For each candidate, incrementally subtract\nits frozen prefix's sufficient statistics at the three required budgets. Refit\nthe identical ridge objective, dividing the data loss by the retained row count,\nnot the original count. The supplied ridge coefficient never changes. Scores\nare centered, Newton directions use Cholesky solves, and backtracking accepts\nsufficient objective descent or a roundoff-sized objective change with improved\ngradient residual. Each fit has at most 100 Newton iterations, matching the\nonly accepted `max_iterations` request value. A fit is usable only with finite\nscores and gradient and gradient infinity norm at most `1e-9`.\n\nWarm-start the first positive budget from clean scores and later budgets from\nthe preceding successful refit. Cache scores by the canonical set of removed\nrow positions, including the empty prefix, so identical prefixes reuse their\nfit across candidates and budgets. Duplicate budgets still contribute once\nper requested fraction to the objective. Failures are cached as failures and\nnever interpreted as exact scores. These positions identify supplied rows only;\nthey do not infer design, question, or judge labels.\n\nFor candidates with successful fits at every requested budget, maximize:\n\n1. Sum of original-leader rank drops using refitted scores rounded to eight\n   decimals and participant-ID tie breaking.\n2. Number of refitted target gaps below `-1e-8`.\n3. Sum of target-gap closure fractions clipped to `[0, 2]`, with denominator\n    ack(call({'op':'release'}))\n    return value,metadata['token']\n\n\ndef load_data(smoke):\n    root = pathlib.Path(os.environ.get('TASK_SOURCE_DIR',pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent))/'resources'/PLANE\n    datasets = {}\n    for family in ('arena','nba'):\n        manifest = json.loads((root/(family+'_manifest.json')).read_text())\n        raw = (root/(family+'.json')).read_bytes()\n        if hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()!=manifest['payload_sha256'] or manifest['plane']!=PLANE:\n            raise ValueError('resource integrity failed')\n        payload = json.loads(raw)\n        if manifest['cross_plane_content_intersection']!=0 or manifest['cross_plane_source_id_intersection']!=0:\n            raise ValueError('content split audit failed')\n        for record in payload['provenance']:\n            code = hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(['split-v1-20261027',family,record['group']],ensure_ascii=False,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest()\n            if (int(code,16)%100<30)!=(PLANE=='search'):\n                raise ValueError('split membership failed')\n        rows = np.array(payload['rows'],dtype=np.float64)\n        groups = np.array([record['group'] for record in payload['provenance']])\n        players = len(payload['participants'])\n        if smoke:\n            exposure = np.bincount(rows[:,:2].astype(int).ravel(),minlength=players)\n            selected = [int(np.argmax(exposure))]\n            while len(selected)<min(12,players):\n                neighbor = np.isin(rows[:,0],selected)^np.isin(rows[:,1],selected)\n                candidates = np.bincount(rows[neighbor,:2].astype(int).ravel(),minlength=players)\n                candidates[selected] = -1\n                if candidates.max()<=0:\n                    break\n                selected.append(int(np.argmax(candidates)))\n            selected = sorted(selected)\n            keep = np.isin(rows[:,0],selected)&np.isin(rows[:,1],selected)\n            rows,groups = rows[keep][:1024],groups[keep][:1024]\n            mapping = {old:new for new,old in enumerate(selected)}\n            rows[:,0] = [mapping[int(value)] for value in rows[:,0]]\n            rows[:,1] = [mapping[int(value)] for value in rows[:,1]]\n            players = len(selected)\n        if not 2<=players<=256 or not 100<=len(rows)<=100000 or len(set(rows[:,3]))!=len(rows):\n            raise ValueError('invalid observed data shape')\n        datasets[family] = (rows,players,groups)\n    return datasets\n\n\ndef final_uncertainty(outcomes,episodes,datasets,deadline,smoke):\n    bootstrap = np.random.default_rng(709237)\n    seeds = list(dict.fromkeys(episode['seed'] for episode in episodes))\n    intervals = {}\n    for name,short in [('paired_gain_vs_random','random'),('paired_gain_vs_disagreement','disagreement')]:\n        means = [sum(outcomes[index][name] for index,episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['seed']==seed)/4 for seed in seeds]\n        samples = bootstrap.choice(means,size=(8 if smoke else 256,len(seeds)),replace=True).mean(axis=1)\n        intervals['paired_gain_'+short+'_ci_low'] = float(np.quantile(samples,.025))\n        intervals['paired_gain_'+short+'_ci_high'] = float(np.quantile(samples,.975))\n    group_results = {}\n    valid = True\n    for family in ('arena','nba'):\n        index = next(index for index,episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['family']==family and not episode['permuted'])\n        solution = outcomes[index]['solution']\n        rows,players,groups = datasets[family]\n        unique,inverse = np.unique(groups,return_inverse=True)\n        records = []\n        for repetition in range(2 if smoke else 32):\n            result = {'candidate':0.,'random':1.,'disagreement':1.,'gain_random':-1.,'gain_disagreement':-1.,'complete':False}\n            if solution is not None:\n                weights = np.bincount(bootstrap.integers(0,len(unique),size=len(unique)),minlength=len(unique))[inverse].astype(float)\n                try:\n                    clean = trusted_fit(rows,players,deadline,weights)\n                    for method in ('candidate','random','disagreement'):\n                        scores = []\n                        for mask in solution[method+'_masks']:\n                            retained = weights.copy(); retained[np.isin(rows[:,3],mask)] = 0\n                            fitted = trusted_fit(rows,players,deadline,retained)\n                            scores.append(disruption(clean,fitted)[0])\n                        result[method] = sum(scores)/3\n                    result['gain_random'] = result['candidate']-result['random']\n                    result['gain_disagreement'] = result['candidate']-result['disagreement']\n                    result['complete'] = True\n                except (TimeoutError,RuntimeError):\n                    result.update(candidate=0.,random=1.,disagreement=1.,gain_random=-1.,gain_disagreement=-1.,complete=False)\n                    valid = False\n            else:\n                valid = False\n            records.append(result)\n        group_results[family] = records\n    return intervals,group_results,valid\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--program_path',required=True)\n    parser.add_argument('--results_dir',required=True)\n                    return trusted_fit(data,players,limit,weights)\n                except (TimeoutError,RuntimeError) as error:\n                    category = 'baseline_timeout' if isinstance(error,TimeoutError) else 'baseline_result_failure'\n                    baseline_failed = True\n                    raise RequiredBaselineFailure(category) from None\n            shared_deadline = reserved_method_deadline(now=time.monotonic(),episode_deadline=deadline,methods_remaining=4,work_seconds=method_work,cleanup_seconds=.6)\n            clean = baseline_fit(canonical,shared_deadline)\n            controls = [False]*4\n            design = matrix(canonical,players)\n            constant_gradient = quantities(np.zeros(players),design,canonical[:,2])[1]\n            if np.max(np.abs(constant_gradient))>2e-7:\n                constant = {'theta':[0.]*players,'contender':int(ranking(clean)[1]),'direction':[0.]*players,\n                            'influence':[0.]*len(rows),'deletions':[[],[],[]]}\n                try:\n                    validate_certificate(constant,canonical,players,clean)\n                except ScientificInvalid:\n                    controls[1] = True\n            method_masks = {}\n            curves = {}; leader_curves = {}\n            rng = np.random.default_rng(episode['seed'])\n            random_order = rng.permutation(len(canonical))\n            margins = design@clean\n            losses = np.logaddexp(0,margins)-canonical[:,2]*margins\n            disagreement_order = np.lexsort((canonical[:,3],-losses))\n            orders = {'random':random_order,'disagreement':disagreement_order}\n            for method_index,method in enumerate(('random','disagreement','copy','candidate')):\n                method_deadline = reserved_method_deadline(now=time.monotonic(),episode_deadline=deadline,methods_remaining=3-method_index,work_seconds=method_work,cleanup_seconds=.6)\n                with time_bound(method_deadline):\n                    if method=='candidate':\n                        value,previous_token = solve_candidate(call,rows,players,previous_token)\n                        try:\n                            theta,masks = validate_certificate(value,rows,players,clean)\n                        except (TypeError,ValueError,IndexError,OverflowError) as error:\n                            raise ProtocolError('malformed certificate') from error\n                        controls[2] = True\n                    elif method=='copy':\n                        masks = [[],[],[]]\n                    else:\n                        masks = [[int(key) for key in canonical[orders[method][:int(fraction*len(canonical))],3]] for fraction in FRACTIONS]\n                    method_masks[method] = masks\n                    scores = []; drops = []\n                    for mask in masks:\n                        retained = canonical[~np.isin(canonical[:,3],mask)]\n                        if method=='candidate':\n                            try:\n                                fitted = trusted_fit(retained,players,method_deadline)\n                            except RuntimeError as error:\n                                raise ProtocolError('candidate perturbation refit invalid') from error\n                        else:\n                            fitted = baseline_fit(retained,method_deadline)\n                        score,drop = disruption(clean,fitted)\n                        scores.append(score); drops.append(drop)\n                    curves[method] = scores; leader_curves[method] = drops\n            controls[0] = curves['copy']==[0.,0.,0.] and leader_curves['copy']==[0.,0.,0.]\n            key = (episode['seed'],episode['family'])\n            if not episode['permuted']:\n                matched[key] = {'theta':theta,'masks':method_masks['candidate'],'curves':curves['candidate']}\n            else:\n                reference = matched.get(key)\n                controls[3] = reference is not None and bool(np.max(np.abs(theta-reference['theta']))<2e-5) and all(set(first)==set(second) for first,second in zip(method_masks['candidate'],reference['masks'])) and bool(np.max(np.abs(np.array(curves['candidate'])-reference['curves']))<1e-8)\n            result = worst_case(episode)\n            result.update(combined_score=sum(curves['candidate'])/3,random_baseline_score=sum(curves['random'])/3,\n                disagreement_baseline_score=sum(curves['disagreement'])/3,\n                paired_gain_vs_random=sum(first-second for first,second in zip(curves['candidate'],curves['random']))/3,\n                paired_gain_vs_disagreement=sum(first-second for first,second in zip(curves['candidate'],curves['disagreement']))/3,\n                mean_leader_rank_drop=sum(leader_curves['candidate'])/3,completion_rate=1.,controls=controls,duration=time.monotonic()-begin,\n                solution={'family':episode['family'],'permuted':episode['permuted'],'curves':curves,'candidate_masks':method_masks['candidate'],\n                          'random_masks':method_masks['random'],'disagreement_masks':method_masks['disagreement'],'clean_scores':clean.tolist()})\n            return result\n        def record_episode_failure(failure):\n            record_failure(failure)\n            try:\n                client.close(failed=True)\n{\n  \"cases\": [\n    {\n      \"family\": \"arena\",\n      \"permuted\": false,\n      \"curves\": {\n        \"candidate\": [\n          0.005952380952380952,\n          0.008432539682539682,\n          0.008928571428571428\n        ],\n        \"copy\": [\n          0.0,\n          0.0,\n          0.0\n        ],\n        \"disagreement\": [\n          0.001488095238095238,\n          0.010416666666666666,\n          0.01636904761904762\n        ],\n        \"random\": [\n          0.0,\n          0.002976190476190476,\n          0.005952380952380952\n        ]\n      },\n      \"players\": 64\n    },\n    {\n      \"family\": \"arena\",\n      \"permuted\": true,\n      \"curves\": {\n        \"candidate\": [\n          0.005952380952380952,\n          0.008432539682539682,\n          0.008928571428571428\n        ],\n        \"copy\": [\n          0.0,\n          0.0,\n          0.0\n        ],\n        \"disagreement\": [\n          0.001488095238095238,\n          0.010416666666666666,\n          0.01636904761904762\n        ],\n        \"random\": [\n          0.0,\n          0.002976190476190476,\n          0.005952380952380952\n        ]\n      },\n      \"players\": 64\n    },\n    {\n      \"family\": \"nba\",\n      \"permuted\": false,\n      \"curves\": {\n        \"candidate\": [\n          0.011477230655312847,\n          0.012587930396149574,\n          0.022954461310625694\n  