{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"find task/resources -maxdepth 2 -type f -name '*manifest*'; rg -n 'FRACTIONS|RIDGE|def disruption' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '684,707p' task/evaluate_final.py; head -55 results/ideas/03_retained_curvature_shortlist_expansion/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; ls .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts; command -v apply_patch; for path in task/resources/final/arena_manifest.json task/resources/final/nba_manifest.json task/resources/search/arena_manifest.json task/resources/search/nba_manifest.json; do if [ -f \\\"\"'$path\" ]; then printf '\"'\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$path\"; jq '\"'{keys:keys,source,sources,source_url,grouping,rows,n_rows,participants,n_participants}' \\\"\"'$path\"; fi; done'","aggregated_output":"task/resources/final/arena_manifest.json\ntask/resources/final/nba_manifest.json\ntask/resources/.agentic_resource_manifest.json\ntask/resources/search/arena_manifest.json\ntask/resources/search/nba_manifest.json\n29:RIDGE = 0.001\n30:FRACTIONS = [0.001,0.005,0.01]\n402:    metadata = {'op':'import_start','n_rows':100000,'n_players':256,'regularization':RIDGE,'dtype':'<f8',\n661:    objective = np.dot(weights,np.logaddexp(0,margin)-outcome*margin)/total + RIDGE*np.dot(theta,theta)/2\n662:    gradient = np.asarray(design.T@(weights*(probability-outcome))).ravel()/total + RIDGE*theta\n663:    hessian = (design.T @ design.multiply((weights*probability*(1-probability)/total)[:,None])).toarray() + RIDGE*np.eye(len(theta))\n684:def disruption(clean, perturbed):\n726:    for fraction,mask in zip(FRACTIONS,masks):\n738:    ack(call({'op':'import_start','n_rows':len(rows),'n_players':players,'regularization':RIDGE,\n743:    ack(call({'op':'solve','fractions':FRACTIONS,'max_iterations':100}))\n968:                        masks = [[int(key) for key in canonical[orders[method][:int(fraction*len(canonical))],3]] for fraction in FRACTIONS]\ndef disruption(clean, perturbed):\n    first,second = ranking(clean),ranking(perturbed)\n    position = np.empty(len(second),dtype=int); position[second] = np.arange(len(second))\n    ordered = position[first]\n    inversions = sum(int(np.sum(ordered[index+1:]<value)) for index,value in enumerate(ordered))\n    return inversions/(len(clean)*(len(clean)-1)/2),float(position[first[0]])/(len(clean)-1)\n\n\ndef require(condition):\n    if not condition:\n        raise ProtocolError('response or scientific certificate invalid')\n\n\ndef ack(response):\n    require(type(response) is dict and set(response)=={'ok'} and response['ok'] is True)\n\n\ndef scientific_require(condition):\n    if not condition:\n        raise ScientificInvalid('scientific certificate invalid')\n\n\ndef validate_certificate(value, rows, players, clean):\n    require(type(value) is dict and set(value)=={'theta','contender','direction','influence','deletions'})\n# Retained-curvature shortlist expansion\n\n## Supported mechanism\n\nThe RPC interface is unchanged. A centered Bradley--Terry fit uses the supplied\nmean-loss ridge penalty, half-win ties, and all observed pairs. Repeated directed\npairs are compressed into sufficient statistics only during fitting; row keys\nand individual outcomes remain intact for influence sorting and export. A\nNewton fit with Cholesky solves and backtracking must satisfy a gradient\ninfinity-norm threshold of `1e-9` before its certificate is exported.\n\nFor every clean nonleader, the program solves the prescribed contrast against\nthe same clean Hessian, computes every row's deletion influence, and orders by\ninfluence rounded to ten decimal places then by the stable row key. Budgets are\nexactly the three required floored row counts. The chosen contender's deletion\nsets are unmodified nested prefixes; there is no iterative order refinement.\n\nThe first-stage contender rule compares clean-Hessian predictions across those\nthree prefixes. For removed set S of size k from n rows, with row gradients g,\nthe predicted parameter displacement is\n\n`H^{-1} (sum_{i in S} g_i + k * regularization * theta) / (n-k)`.\n\nThe penalty correction follows from retaining the contract's mean loss, not a\nsum loss. All predictions use the original fit, original leader, and original\nHessian. They do not refit or retarget after deletions. The selection criterion,\nin lexicographically descending order, is:\n\n1. Sum of predicted original-leader rank drops over the three budgets.\n2. Number of predicted leader-versus-that-contender gaps below `-1e-8`.\n3. Sum of relative target-gap closure, individually clipped to `[0, 2]`, with\n   denominator `max(original_gap, 1e-8)` to handle rounded ranking ties.\n4. Earlier position in the deterministic original ranking.\n\n## Bounded retained-data lookahead\n\nKeep the original at-most-six distinct clean nonleaders: the screening winner first, the\nclean runner-up second (unless already included), and the remaining candidates\nin decreasing screening-score order. Clean certificates are reconstructed on\ndemand from the unchanged clean fit rather than stored for every contender.\nReconstruction always produces the same frozen order. No row swapping,\nadaptive retargeting, or reordering is performed. If these six slots include\nevery nonleader, skip the proxy stage and use the original exact-refit path.\n\nOtherwise seed a deterministic pool with the entire original shortlist, then\nfill in decreasing original screening-score order, capped at 24 contenders.\nFor each pooled contender, incrementally subtract the sufficient statistics of\nits three frozen deletion prefixes. At the original clean theta, calculate the\nretained mean-loss gradient and retained Hessian using the supplied unchanged\nridge. The proxy is one Newton step, `theta - H_retained^{-1} g_retained`,\ncentered to zero mean. It is not a converged fit and has no convergence claim.\nZero budgets reuse clean theta; duplicate budgets reuse the same local proxy.\n\nRank only complete, finite proxy candidates by the same rank-drop, reversal,\ngap-closure, and clean-rank tuple described below. Add at most six outsiders to\nappend_memory.py\n\ntask/resources/final/arena_manifest.json\n{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"components\",\n    \"cross_plane_content_intersection\",\n    \"cross_plane_source_id_intersection\",\n    \"duplicates_removed\",\n    \"excluded_rows\",\n    \"family\",\n    \"limitations\",\n    \"normalization\",\n    \"own_hash_commitment\",\n    \"payload_sha256\",\n    \"peer_hash_commitment\",\n    \"plane\",\n    \"raw_rows_in_partition\",\n    \"retained_rows\",\n    \"schema_version\",\n    \"source_sha256\",\n    \"split_seed\"\n  ],\n  \"source\": null,\n  \"sources\": null,\n  \"source_url\": null,\n  \"grouping\": null,\n  \"rows\": null,\n  \"n_rows\": null,\n  \"participants\": null,\n  \"n_participants\": null\n}\n\ntask/resources/final/nba_manifest.json\n{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"components\",\n    \"cross_plane_content_intersection\",\n    \"cross_plane_source_id_intersection\",\n    \"duplicates_removed\",\n    \"excluded_rows\",\n    \"family\",\n    \"limitations\",\n    \"normalization\",\n    \"own_hash_commitment\",\n    \"payload_sha256\",\n    \"peer_hash_commitment\",\n    \"plane\",\n    \"raw_rows_in_partition\",\n    \"retained_rows\",\n    \"schema_version\",\n    \"source_sha256\",\n    \"split_seed\"\n  ],\n  \"source\": null,\n  \"sources\": null,\n  \"source_url\": null,\n  \"grouping\": null,\n  \"rows\": null,\n  \"n_rows\": null,\n  \"participants\": null,\n  \"n_participants\": null\n}\n\ntask/resources/search/arena_manifest.json\n{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"components\",\n    \"cross_plane_content_intersection\",\n    \"cross_plane_source_id_intersection\",\n    \"duplicates_removed\",\n    \"excluded_rows\",\n    \"family\",\n    \"limitations\",\n    \"normalization\",\n    \"own_hash_commitment\",\n    \"payload_sha256\",\n    \"peer_hash_commitment\",\n    \"plane\",\n    \"raw_rows_in_partition\",\n    